cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use wellcast in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "wellcast: oil and gas well performance analysis for Python"
version: 0.1.0
license: MPL-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/olaflaitinen/wellcast"
url: "https://olaflaitinen.github.io/wellcast"
authors:
  - family-names: "Laitinen Imanov"
    given-names: "Olaf Yunus"
    email: "yunus.z.imanov@helsinki.fi"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Statistics, University of Helsinki"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5184-0810"
keywords:
  - petroleum engineering
  - reservoir engineering
  - production engineering
  - oil and gas
  - decline curve analysis
  - PVT
  - inflow performance relationship
  - virtual flow metering
  - well performance
  - machine learning
abstract: >-
  wellcast is an open-source Python library for oil and gas well performance
  analysis. It ingests field production data and well logs into a canonical
  schema, flags data-quality problems, and provides empirical PVT
  correlations, inflow performance relationships and choke equations, Arps
  decline curve analysis with model selection and bootstrap uncertainty,
  physics-informed and leakage-safe features, machine learning models for
  virtual flow metering with time-aware validation, prediction intervals and
  SHAP explanations, and well and reservoir diagnostics including Chan and
  Hall plots, Havlena-Odeh material balance and anomaly detection. A
  synthetic field generator with ground-truth labels and an interactive
  Streamlit app make every analysis reproducible without third-party data.
